        "created_at": "2025-10-01T21:27:10.508Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It’s been literally years since I worked with a log of a SOTM app game, and I was on a different type of device back then, but I know there’s a way of accessing the most recent such log, and the game I just had NEEDS to be shared with those few of us that are still reading here.  It was an Ultimate (non-Cosmic) Omnitron game against Benchmark, Mainstay, Luminary and Setback, in Madame Mittermaier’s Fantastical Festival of Conundrums and Curiosities.  And I swear, the whole game was an experiment Luminary was running to figure out what Setback’s deal is, until the two less-nice actual heroes get tired of Ivan’s crap and start actively destroying his devices, not least because the Omnitron code is hiding in them.  But meanwhile, Setback is locked in the Freak Show, billed as the Incredible Quantum Uncertainty Man, endlessly playing All-Seeing Alzrabar like it’s a Mortal Kombat arcade cabinet in 1993, constantly in a superposition of being able or unable to deal damage to himself, so that despite being reduced quite early to 1 HP, he never actually dies.</p>\n<p>You see why I need to share every detail of this game with the forum.  But I don’t remember (slash never knew) where to look for the recent game log (on my Windows computer).  I can’t play the app again until I get this info, for fear of deleting the automatic log!  Please Obi-Wan Kenobi, if you would be so kind.</p>",
